         BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION

 IN THE MATTER OF THE APPLICATION OF                        )
 EL PASO ELECTRIC COMPANY FOR                               )
 REVISION OF ITS RETAIL ELECTRIC RATES                      )    Docket No. 25-00082-UT
 PURSUANT TO ADVICE NOTICE NO. 317                          )


                               SECOND PROCEDURAL ORDER

       THIS MATTER comes before Jocelyn Barrett and Elizabeth C. Hurst, Hearing Examiners

for the New Mexico Public Regulation Commission (“Commission”), in the above-captioned

Application for Revision of Electric Rates of El Paso Electric Company (“EPE”), and the

Commission’s Rules of Procedure 1.2.2.24 and 1.2.2.29 NMAC. Being duly informed, the Hearing

Examiners FIND AND CONCLUDE:

   1. On March 27, 2026, EPE filed its Application for Revision of Retail Electric Rates under

Advice Notice No. 317 containing EPE’s proposed rates. On April 8, 2026, EPE filed a Notice of

Filing of Supplemental Schedule Q-6 – The Independent Accountant’s Review Report for EPE for

the calendar year 2024. On April 15, 2026, EPE filed a Notice of Errata and Filing of Replacement

Exhibits (“Notice of Errata”). In the Notice of Errata, EPE stated it discovered or was made aware

that there were several errors in its initial Application filing. Specifically, the errors included: a

wrong document filed, incorrect formatting, and, most significantly, missing workpapers. EPE

requested the corrected pages attached to its Notice of Errata, which amounted to over 1,600 pages,

are substituted for the incorrect versions filed with EPE’s Application.

   2. On April 27, 2026, the Hearing Examiners issued a Procedural Order and Notice for this

case. Paragraph “Q” of the Procedural Order requires “all filings shall be emailed to the Hearing

Examiners in Word or other native version of the filing if created in such format.
            BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION
Second Procedural Order                              Docket No. 25-00082-UT


   3. On June 20, 2026, EPE provided a link to a server for the Hearing Examiners to access the

native files of their Application.

   4. The Hearing Examiners find it necessary to amend their Procedural Order paragraph “Q”

to require that in addition to the Hearing Examiners, emails of or access to all filings in native

format in this case shall be provided to the Commission’s Technical Advisor, Andrew Nelson, and

Assistant General Counsel Alyssa Herrera-Waldroup.

    IT IS THEREFORE ORDERED:

    A. The Procedural Order paragraph “Q” is amended to require emails of or access to all filings

in native format in this case shall be provided to the Commission’s Technical Advisor, Andrew

Nelson, and Assistant General Counsel Alyssa Herrera-Waldroup.

    B. All parts of the Procedural Order issued on April 27, 2026, not modified by this Second

Procedural, are in full force and effect.

    ISSUED under the seal of the Commission at Santa Fe, New Mexico, this 22nd day of June

2026.

                       NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION



                       Elizabeth C. Hurst
                       Hearing Examiner
                       elizabeth.hurst@prc.nm.gov




                                               -2-
